    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d480">

                <pb facs="0548" n="536" sameAs="frus:frus1944v03/pg536"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">859.01/167: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in the United Kingdom</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Bucknell</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">London</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1944-05-20T17:00:00+02:00">May 20, 1944—5
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received 8:35 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>4079. Reference Embassy’s 3892, May 13, 2 p.m.<anchor n="30" xml:id="d480-f1"/> A
                    communication has been received from the Foreign Office stating that a telegram
                    has now been received from Moscow to the effect that the British Ambassador sent
                    the draft declaration on Denmark to M. Vyshinski<anchor n="31" xml:id="d480-f2"
                    /> on May 9. In accordance with an arrangement with the American Chargé, who
                    wrote Vyshinski May 10, the British Ambassador’s letter <pb facs="0549" n="537"
                        xml:id="pg537"/> made no mention of the prior clearance of the declaration
                    with the King of Denmark.</p>
                <p>As a result of further telegrams from the F.O. regarding proposed arrangements
                    for publication, the British Ambassador has again written to M. Vyshinski
                    stressing the urgency of the matter and he proposes to remind the Soviets
                    again.</p>
                <p>Repeated to Moscow.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Bucknell</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d480-f1" n="30" xml:id="d480-f1-content">
                <p>Not printed.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d480-f2" n="31" xml:id="d480-f2-content">
                <p>Andrey Yanuaryevich Vyshinsky, First Assistant People’s Commissar for Foreign
                    Affairs of the Soviet Union.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
